# Catalog Security

## Secrets and Sensitive Data

- Never hardcode API keys, tokens, or passwords in `js/data.js`, HTML, or scripts.
- Never paste secrets into agent prompts or commit messages.
- Keep `.env`, keys, and credentials out of the public site and out of git.
- If a secret was exposed, rotate it before continuing.

## Content Pipeline Safety

- Public pages and `js/data.js` must reference only `assets/<case-id>/...`, never `inbox/`.
- Do not ship raw client uploads or private filenames without review.
- Verify CTA links (`tel:`, `https://`) before publishing a case.

## Shell and Git Safety

- Do not bypass git hooks with `--no-verify` or `core.hooksPath` overrides.
- Ask for confirmation before destructive commands (`git reset --hard`, `rm -rf`, forced deletes).
- Do not commit `.cursor/skills/**/__pycache__` or other build artifacts.

## Before Publishing

- Run `python scripts/validate-cases.py` after data or asset changes.
- Spot-check case pages for broken media, leaked internal paths, and wrong contact links.
